      "writtenOn": "2021-09-30T08:07:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Technically condition #1 is not difficult to trigger, just send a packet or make an HTTP request. A UDP packet to 8.8.8.8 and/or 2001:4860:4860::8888 port 9 (or whatever other port) should cause the callback to fire if the network is inactive.\n\nHowever, since there\u0027s no notification for when the network becomes *inactive*, it seems like it would be difficult to write a test for it, because until the network becomes inactive, sending a packet won\u0027t cause it to become active.",
